ning it's a little sci-fi a  little action and all awesome the hunter  ever wanted to watch willem dafoe hunt  for an extinct tiger in the wilds of  tasmania well the hunter has just made  your dreams come true  this unusual action film combines  science exotic locales and rich  character depths to create a really  intriguing action movie  if you're looking for a slower pace but  extremely well acted action adventure  the hunter is just the ticket lucky  number Slevin this quirky crime comedy  flew under the radar on its release but  lucky number Slevin is full of twists  turns and distracting funds that'll keep  you watching to the end it's clever  funny and has an amazing cast that  includes Morgan Freeman Bruce Willis  Lucy Liu and Ben Kingsley with a clever  script and slick visual style lucky  number Slevin is surprisingly  entertaining  the finest hours based on a true story  the tale of a daring 1952 Coast Guard  rescue received some pretty positive  reviews but kind of sank after its  initial release maybe because the finest  hours is pretty generic for a title but  this real-life tale starring Star Trek's  Chris Pine is full of thrilling moments  and moving drama so before the finest  hours slipped from your memory again  give this fine historical drama a try  alive this gripping drama is based on  the true story of a Uruguayan rugby team  struggling to survive in the Andes after  a plane crash after only twenty-five  people lived through the initial  accident the team members have to resort  to desperate measures to stay alive if  you haven't already guessed yes this is  the movie where the survivors end up  eating each other but it's not a horror  film watching these people grasp at hope  through the very worst conditions is  harrowing and although the movie sounds  kind of depressing is actually an  uplifting tale of survival and the  unbelievable strength of mankind not to  mention a roller coaster ride of sheer  adrenaline sufers just in case two  installments of guardians of the galaxy  wasn't enough to satisfy your love of  james gunn films netflix has a classic  waiting for you before you watch super  guns for a superhero film you should  know that it's a dark comedy very dark  that said it's definitely a visually  unique take on superheroes starring  Rainn Wilson and Ellen Page super is  about a man who decides to dress up as a  superhero to save his ex-wife who  doesn't really want to be saved it may  not have the budget of guardians but you  can see Gunn's flair for action and  irreverent humor shine through troll  hunter this surprisingly unique film  follows a group of  people on a quest to find real trolls in  the frozen tundra of Norway after they  find out that the existence of trolls  has been covered up by the Norwegian  government they make it their duty to  capture one of the elusive monsters on  film this is no troll sue these trolls  look amazing and don't have to turn  humans into plans to eat them shot like  a documentary the film is often  hilarious though not without its tense  moments moira macdonald film critic at  The Seattle Times wrote those fog drapes  fjords provide a distractingly pretty  backdrop to this tale of mysterious  massive creatures who roam the forests  by night searching for Christians on  whom to munch it's safe to say that  you're not going to find a better movie  about massive monsters eating religious  folks zombeavers don't worry zombie  earth is completely aware that it's a  movie about zombie beavers thankfully  it's a fun horror parody that makes the  idea of undead beavers as funny as it  could possibly be critic Tim Brighton  called it the funniest horror comedy  since at the very least the cabin in the  woods if you want a campy diverting  comedy that's full of laughs and  gross-out gags zombeavers is exactly  what you're looking for welcome to the  punch starring mark Strong and James  McAvoy as a criminal and cop who team  ups you uncover a conspiracy  welcome to the plunge is straight-up  action in the best possible way the  solid casting choices lend a bit of  seriousness and depth of character to  the storage but let's all be honest this  is a movie you watch for often change  scenes and gun fights welcome to the  punch is pretty violence but you'd  probably expect that from a film that  invites you to a beating in the title  last night a cast that stars Clive Owen  and Morgan Freeman usually means a movie  worth watching add in castles swords and  revenge and you have yourself a fine  action film now the critics weren't  especially kind to last night but the  New York Times thought bonnie-and-clyde  was an overly violent pointless piece of  cinema but why listened to critics last  night's probably won't stand the test of  time like Bonnie and Clyde  but it's Game of Thrones reruns aren't  doing it for you or if you just like  hearing the soothing tones of Morgan  Freeman while people are killed with  swords slash sights is worth a watch  thanks for watching click the  four icons to subscribe to our YouTube  channel plus check out all this cool  stuff we know you'll love to  [Music]

